WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
 Well, I'm a huge fan of Live Healthy

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.220
 Chicago, first of all.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:07.320
 I think hypertension is really, really

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.590
 important as a driver of the life

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.400
 expectancy gap in

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.260
 Chicago, and it's really important that

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.860
 we do a better job from a community

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.760
 perspective,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.460
 from a public health perspective, and

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.970
 from in the office, in the hospital

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.640
 perspective

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.200
 of controlling hypertension.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.960
 At Rush, in my role, I work with all of

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.140
 our community teams where we're bringing

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:28.480
 care

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.720
 to where people are.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.580
 So instead of expecting people to come to

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.080
 Rush, we go to where they are.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.340
 And so that's why I'm really proud of the

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.480
 Live Healthy Chicago mobile team for

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.120
 diagnosing

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.980
 and treating hypertension where people

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.200
 live, work, and play.

